 not  [Music]  this recipe is so good for how  shockingly easy it is you should try  this but if you think this looks good  wait until the next recipe this next  method involves pan frying to make  peanut butter and jelly fritters i like  these because they're super versatile  you can use them as breakfast lunch a  snack dinner dessert whatever you want  these are sort of like homemade  uncrustables except they're entirely  surrounded by crust crustables now to  get started i'm actually going to flour  my work surface a little bit just so  that my biscuit dough doesn't stick i'm  going to take two biscuits roll these  out until they're nice and thin and  about five inches in diameter i'm going  to add peanut butter to one and then i'm  going to do the same thing with the  jelly take a little bit of water and  apply it to the outsides of the dough  and this is going to help make the seal  that we use to keep all of our toppings  inside so now it's time to very gently  put our sides together i'm gonna go with  the peanut butter one because i find the  peanut butter is thicker it doesn't run  as much as the jelly would i'm just  going to drop these two on each other  look at that and you really want to seal  this bad boy up because if you don't it  will leak and you'll get jelly all over  your pan and you'll have to make another  one and we don't want that and i'm just  going to punch out my little pb j  fritter i'm using a biscuit cutter here  you can use a cup just anything that's  big enough to cut all the way around wow  look at that pop it in the fridge for  about 30 minutes this is just really  going to let the seal come together my  pan has been heated over medium-low heat  just adding a little bit of ghee and the  reason you should use ghee for this is  the chance it can burn and ghee has a  higher smoke point and just place it  right down in my pan don't touch this  just let it go for about four to five  minutes i can tell it's nice and brown  on the bottom because the edges are  toasted which means it's time to flip  and  wow just repeat what you did with the  last step let it go for about three to  four more minutes and that my friends is  a peanut butter and jelly fritter before  i dig in i do want to elevate it a  little bit i'm adding a little bit of  powdered sugar this is totally optional  cut this guy in half  let's see what this guy is all about  these are a nice treat they're crunchy  on the outside they're nice and fluffy  on the inside they're gooey towards the  middle where the peanut butter and the  jelly kind of ooze out these are great  as a snack or can be enjoyed any time of  day these first two recipes have been  great but for number three we're  thinking a little bit out of the box  we're at the halfway point so we're  going to be using a steamer to make  biscuit bow buns i used to live next to  a shop that sold bow buns and they are  literally the best thing i would go all  of the time rather than using regular  biscuit dough this is actually the flaky  variety and that's what works with this  recipe and i'm just going to flatten  these out a little bit maybe about four  inches or so across  and this next step is optional but just  because i like things to be uniform when  i'm cooking i'm actually going to use a  glass here to kind of punch out a shape  i'm just going to add a little bit of  cooking spray  fold  each one of my biscuits in half and  there you have it four biscuit bowl buns  that's a tongue twister ready to go my  heat is cranked to medium high i have a  pot of water here coming to a boil over  it i have my steaming basket let's see  if we're ready  and i'm going to layer in my boughs  and this is going to go for about five  to seven minutes until nice and puffy  watch for steam  oh my goodness look at how puffy  delicately remove from the heat  after a few minutes your buns are going  to start to settle a little bit don't  let them sit for too long because when  they deflate all the way they're really  no good you can fill them with whatever  you'd like i'm going to be filling mine  with an assortment of pickled vegetables  pork belly some cilantro and mint and  there you are biscuit bowl buns  now it's not exactly like authentic bow  it doesn't have the same taste it's a  little bit more buttery it works so well  the bun is so light and fluffy it holds  everything so perfectly i really really  encourage you to try this it's time to  boil our dough to make mini pretzel  bites these are a super fun little snack  you can dunk it into whatever you want  they're great for a party they're great  for kids they're just really fun to get  started much like with the last recipe  we're going to be using flaky biscuits  for this cut them  into four equal-ish pieces and once your  biscuits are nice and cut up you're just  gonna roll them into little balls just  like that  so i have here a pot of boiling water  boom to which i'm going to add about  half a cup of baking soda bubble bubble  toil and treble cool so now that those  are combined the next couple steps  happen pretty quickly i'm going to take  my biscuits and just add them  and i'm just going to let those go for  about 30 seconds and then once they are  floating pull them off and add to a  parchment-lined sheet i'm bending the  rules just a little bit at this point  instead of just boiling these i'm  actually going to throw them in the  airfryer here to get them nice and brown  and crisp on the outside but before that  i'm going to top my little dough balls  with some butter and salt  i'm going to throw these in my air fryer  for about five to seven minutes until  they're done  ho ho baby look at  them oh no  it's okay we'll forget about you and  there they are biscuit dough pretzel  bites you can serve them with whatever  you want i'm actually gonna go with  nacho cheese  these are really good they're ever so  crunchy on the outside they're super  light and fluffy on the inside these are  so much 