cuit you got your hamburger meat  the cheese on top allows it to melt down  and kind of cover everything bon appetit  these are just really good they read  exactly like a burger you've got the  beef you've got the cheese you've got  the ketchup you've got the bun even got  the sesame seeds on top if a  cheeseburger and a dumpling came  together and had a beautiful baby it  would be the cheeseburger bomb we're  wrapping things up today by deep frying  in order to make deep fried frozen ice  cream there's no better way than to end  things on a sweet note and this is a  really fun cool crunchy way of doing  that at least four hours before you do  anything you want to pop your ice cream  balls in the freezer just to make sure  they're frozen solid so they don't melt  while you're working with them in order  to make all of them nice and uniform i  just took a cookie scoop like this and  divided each portion in half toss this  back in the freezer until you're ready  to actually start forming them take six  biscuits and cut each of them in half  and then roll those out as thinly and  uniformly as possible be careful not to  tear the dough or to let it stick in any  way because if you form any holes in  your ice cream it's going to leak out  while you fry it in order to shape the  ice cream balls you need to work really  quickly take one piece of dough and my  advice for handling the ice cream  actually use chopsticks or cold spoon  that way you're minimizing that hot  contact place your ice cream in the  middle and then fold  all the edges  up and you want to make sure that  there's no gaps no nothing no leakage  and there you are just repeat with the  remaining balls these are our 12 perfect  little ice cream balls these need to sit  in the freezer for an additional one to  two hours just to firm everything up i  have good news and i have bad news the  good news is it's time to fry our ice  cream the bad news is we still have a  couple hours to go before we can  actually try it my pot of oil is heated  to 325 degrees fahrenheit and working in  batches i'll add about four frozen ice  cream balls at a time  these are going to cook in the pot for  about two to three minutes until they're  nice and golden brown on the outside  once they're nice and brown just place  them on a paper towel lined baking sheet  to let them drain  now i said there was bad news and that's  because there's one more phase of  waiting these need to go back in the  freezer for an additional hour so they  can firm up again oh my goodness i was  beginning to think we wouldn't get here  now you can top it with whatever you  want i'm gonna go with the classic  chocolate syrup whipped cream and  sprinkles  [Music]  you know something's good you can't even  muster the words to kind of talk while  you're chewing it it's perfectly crunchy  on the outside but then you have the  nice soft cool ice cream on the inside  it takes a lot of time but if someone  gave me this  i would be impressed today i showed you  six ways of using canned biscuit dough  that don't follow the baking  instructions on the package we  microwaved it to make a mug pizza pan  fried it to make pb j fritters steamed  it to make biscuit bow buns boiled it to  make mini pretzel bites grilled it to  make cheeseburger bombs and finally deep  fried it to make deep fried frozen ice  cream let me know which one is your  favorite or if you have another creative  use for biscuit dough let me know in the  comments below or message me on  instagram and until then take care my  friends oh yes  [Music]  do  [Music]

